---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const breadcrumbs = [
{ label: 'Blog', url: '/en/blog/' },
{ label: 'Pet Exercise by Age', url: '/en/blog/pet-exercise-by-age/' }
];
const siteUrl = "https://www.petaginghub.com";
const hrefLangAlternates = [
{ lang: 'zh-TW', url: siteUrl + '/blog/pet-exercise-by-age' },
{ lang: 'en', url: siteUrl + '/en/blog/pet-exercise-by-age' },
{ lang: 'x-default', url: siteUrl + '/blog/pet-exercise-by-age' },
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Pet Exercise Guide by Age - Pet Aging Hub"
description="Age-appropriate activity guides for dogs and cats at every life stage. Too little or too much exercise both cause problems."
lang="en" breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs} hrefLangAlternates={hrefLangAlternates}>
<article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto py-10 px-4">
<header class="mb-8">
<span class="inline-block bg-blue-100 text-blue-700 text-xs font-bold px-3 py-1 rounded-full mb-4">Wellness</span>
<h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 mb-4">Age-Appropriate Exercise for Dogs and Cats</h1>
<p class="text-xl text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">Exercise needs change dramatically as pets age. Too little leads to obesity and muscle loss; too much can cause injury and pain.</p>
</header>
<div class="space-y-10">
<section>
<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-5">Dogs: Exercise by Life Stage</h2>
<div class="space-y-4">
<div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-5 border border-slate-200">
<div class="flex justify-between items-start mb-2">
<h3 class="font-bold text-amber-800">Puppy (0-1 year)</h3>
<span class="text-xs bg-amber-100 text-amber-700 px-2 py-1 rounded-full">5 min per month of age, 2x/day</span>
</div>
<p class="text-slate-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">Over-exercise is a real risk. Avoid forced running until growth plates close (12-18 months). The 5-minute rule: 5 minutes of exercise per month of age, twice a day.</p>
</div>
<div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-5 border border-slate-200">
<div class="flex justify-between items-start mb-2">
<h3 class="font-bold text-amber-800">Adult (1-7 years)</h3>
<span class="text-xs bg-green-100 text-green-700 px-2 py-1 rounded-full">30-60 min/day (breed dependent)</span>
</div>
<p class="text-slate-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">Activity needs vary enormously by breed. A Border Collie needs 2+ hours of vigorous daily exercise; a Bulldog may need 20-30 minutes. Provide both physical exercise and mental stimulation. Combining activity with the right <a href="/en/blog/pet-nutrition-by-age/" class="text-blue-600 underline">pet nutrition for your dog's age</a> is what truly keeps adult dogs in peak condition.</p>
</div>
<div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-5 border border-slate-200">
<div class="flex justify-between items-start mb-2">
<h3 class="font-bold text-amber-800">Senior (7+ years)</h3>
<span class="text-xs bg-blue-100 text-blue-700 px-2 py-1 rounded-full">20-30 min, 2-3x/day (gentle)</span>
</div>
<p class="text-slate-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">Shorter, more frequent walks are better than one long walk. Watch for post-exercise limping, reluctance to get up the next morning, or excessive panting as signs of over-exertion. If your dog shows signs of stiffness, our <a href="/en/blog/pet-joint-health/" class="text-blue-600 underline">pet joint health guide</a> explains management options that can help them stay active longer. For a complete picture of caring for an aging dog, see our <a href="/en/blog/senior-dog-care/" class="text-blue-600 underline">senior dog care guide</a>.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section>
<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-5">Cats: Activity by Life Stage</h2>
<div class="space-y-4">
<div class="bg-purple-50 rounded-2xl p-5 border border-purple-100">
<h3 class="font-bold text-purple-800 mb-2">Kitten (0-1 year)</h3>
<p class="text-slate-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">Multiple play sessions per day (5-10 minutes each). Wand toys, feather toys, and puzzle feeders support physical and mental development.</p>
</div>
<div class="bg-purple-50 rounded-2xl p-5 border border-purple-100">
<h3 class="font-bold text-purple-800 mb-2">Adult (1-10 years)</h3>
<p class="text-slate-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">Two 10-15 minute interactive play sessions per day. Prevent obesity — weigh monthly and adjust food if weight drifts up.</p>
</div>
<div class="bg-purple-50 rounded-2xl p-5 border border-purple-100">
<h3 class="font-bold text-purple-800 mb-2">Senior (10+ years)</h3>
<p class="text-slate-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">Lower-intensity play — gentler wand movements, puzzle feeders, calm sessions. Even 5-minute sessions per day maintain muscle and joint flexibility. Provide ramps so senior cats do not skip enrichment due to mobility issues.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section>
<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">Best Low-Impact Activities for Senior Pets</h2>
<div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
<div class="bg-amber-50 rounded-xl p-4 border border-amber-100">
<h3 class="font-bold text-amber-800 mb-2">Senior Dogs</h3>
<ul class="text-sm text-slate-700 space-y-1">
<li>Gentle leash walks on flat surfaces</li>
<li>Swimming and hydrotherapy</li>
<li>Nose work (scent games)</li>
<li>Short training sessions</li>
<li>Slow-paced fetch on soft grass</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div class="bg-purple-50 rounded-xl p-4 border border-purple-100">
<h3 class="font-bold text-purple-800 mb-2">Senior Cats</h3>
<ul class="text-sm text-slate-700 space-y-1">
<li>Slow wand toy sessions</li>
<li>Puzzle feeders</li>
<li>Cat TV and bird watching setups</li>
<li>Gentle grooming sessions</li>
<li>Hiding treats for searching</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</div>
<div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
<a href="/en/blog/pet-joint-health/" class="px-5 py-3 bg-blue-500 hover:bg-blue-600 text-white font-semibold rounded-xl text-sm">Joint Health Guide</a>
<a href="/en/blog/senior-pet-health-guide/" class="px-5 py-3 bg-slate-100 hover:bg-slate-200 text-slate-800 font-semibold rounded-xl text-sm">Senior Pet Guide</a>
</div>
</article>

<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
"@context": "https://schema.org",
"@type": "FAQPage",
"mainEntity": [
{
"@type": "Question",
"name": "How much exercise does a senior dog need?",
"acceptedAnswer": {
"@type": "Answer",
"text": "Senior dogs (7+ years) generally need 20-30 minutes of gentle exercise, 2-3 times per day. Shorter, more frequent walks are better than one long walk. Watch for post-exercise limping, reluctance to rise the next morning, or excessive panting as signs of over-exertion."
}
},
{
"@type": "Question",
"name": "Can you over-exercise a puppy?",
"acceptedAnswer": {
"@type": "Answer",
"text": "Yes. Over-exercising a puppy is a real risk. Growth plates are still forming until 12-18 months, and forced running or jumping can cause permanent joint damage. Follow the 5-minute rule: 5 minutes of exercise per month of age, twice a day."
}
},
{
"@type": "Question",
"name": "How do I keep my indoor cat active?",
"acceptedAnswer": {
"@type": "Answer",
"text": "Two 10-15 minute interactive play sessions per day with wand toys or puzzle feeders are ideal for adult cats. Senior cats benefit from shorter, gentler sessions — even 5 minutes daily helps maintain muscle and joint flexibility. Ramps can help cats with mobility issues access their favorite spots."
}
},
{
"@type": "Question",
"name": "What low-impact activities are safe for senior dogs?",
"acceptedAnswer": {
"@type": "Answer",
"text": "The best low-impact activities for senior dogs include gentle leash walks on flat surfaces, swimming and hydrotherapy (excellent for arthritic dogs), nose work and scent games, short training sessions for mental stimulation, and slow-paced fetch on soft grass."
}
}
]
})} />

</BaseLayout>
